/**
 * Authoritative statement storage in the existing TripleStore environment. Every method uses the supplied LMDB
 * transaction: there is no current-state cache, independently committed delta log, or asynchronous correctness state.
 *
 * <p>
 * Pages and edge deltas share unsigned lexicographic keys: plane (one byte), raw predicate, row, neighbor, context
 * (four big-endian longs). A page key is its first pair, so a point lookup needs one predecessor seek. Planes 0/1 are
 * explicit outgoing/incoming; 2/3 are inferred outgoing/incoming. Delta values are one byte: present (1) or absent (0).
 * LMDB itself retains earlier versions for readers; each visible delta is the final state of that edge relative to its
 * visible base page. An operation restoring the base state removes its delta.
 *
 * <p>
 * Metadata uses a one-byte type followed by big-endian identifiers. Type 0 is the four-byte format version; 1 is plane
 * total; 2 plane/predicate count; 3 plane/predicate/row count; 4 plane/row/predicate count; 5 plane/context count; 6
 * context count across explicit and inferred statements; 7 value reference count across all quad positions; 8
 * plane/predicate/row delta count; 9 plane/predicate delta count; 10 persistent compaction candidate. Zero counts have
 * no entry. Both row orders are directories, not copies of statements.
 *
 * <p>
 * Compaction merges at most one base page and one bounded delta batch at a time, preserving other page values. Pages,
 * counts, delta deletion, and both directions publish atomically with the surrounding statement transaction.
 */
